│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponentially-weighted moving average (which introduces systematic lag and    │
│                          │ fails to smooth reversals well) with a two-stage approach: (1) a constant-velocity Kalman │
│                          │ filter that adaptively estimates local signal level and slope with measurement-noise      │
│                          │ estimation, and (2) a short Savitzky-Golay-style polynomial smoother applied on top to    │
│                          │ further suppress slope changes and false reversals. The Kalman filter's predictive step   │
│                          │ compensates for the group delay of the smoothing, dramatically reducing lag error while   │
│                          │ the process-noise adaptation preserves genuine trend dynamics (tracking accuracy). Output │
│                          │ is re-indexed to match the existing sliding-window length convention so downstream code   │
│                          │ is unchanged. This addresses all four objectives: fewer spurious slope changes, low lag,  │
│                          │ good trend tracking, and fewer false reversals, while remaining O(N) and fast.            │
