│ patch_description        │ Restructures the filter into a modular three-stage pipeline: (1) a Savitzky-Golay-style   │
│                          │ local quadratic fit evaluated at the window's leading edge for zero-lag trend estimation, │
│                          │ (2) a 1D constant-velocity Kalman filter with innovation-gated adaptive measurement noise │
│                          │ (rejects noise outliers, follows genuine dynamics), and (3) a slope-stability governor    │
│                          │ that damps output only when the estimated slope sign is unstable, directly targeting      │
│                          │ slope changes and false reversals. This separation of estimation, fusion, and             │
│                          │ stabilization concerns improves all four objectives simultaneously and keeps the          │
│                          │ architecture maintainable.                                                                │
