│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponential weighted moving average with a two-stage hybrid: (1) a 1D Kalman  │
│                          │ filter with adaptive measurement noise estimated from local residuals (handles            │
│                          │ non-stationary noise, zero phase lag), and (2) a short Savitzky-Golay smoothing pass      │
│                          │ (polynomial trend preservation, minimal lag). The Kalman filter provides responsiveness   │
│                          │ with minimal lag error, while the SG filter with low order preserves genuine trends and   │
│                          │ reduces slope changes/false reversals. Output length is preserved to match expected       │
│                          │ window-based alignment (len(x) - window_size + 1) by trimming from the front, since       │
│                          │ Kalman estimates align with the most recent sample.                                       │
