│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rts_smoother_zero_phase                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The metrics show the main weakness is smoothness: slope_changes (307) and false_reversals │
│                          │ (245.4) are very high, while lag/accuracy are already good. The current causal Kalman     │
│                          │ filter is noisy because the adaptive measurement noise (r = r_base + 0.5*innov²) makes    │
│                          │ the filter over-trust large innovations (which are often noise spikes), producing         │
│                          │ spurious directional reversals. Two targeted fixes:                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Soften the adaptive R using a smoothed innovation estimate (EMA of squared             │
│                          │ innovations) instead of the instantaneous innovation — this prevents single noise         │
│                          │ outliers from collapsing the measurement noise and yanking the state, which directly      │
│                          │ reduces slope changes and false reversals without adding lag.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Add a forward-backward (Rauch-Tung-Striebel style two-pass) smoothing pass over the    │
│                          │ Kalman estimates. Since this is offline sliding-window processing (we already return a    │
│                          │ windowed output), running the same constant-velocity filter backwards and averaging with  │
│                          │ the forward pass makes the filter effectively zero-phase, eliminating the phase delay of  │
│                          │ the causal filter while suppressing high-frequency jitter — this improves smoothness AND  │
│                          │ reduces lag error simultaneously, without hurting tracking accuracy since both passes use │
│                          │ the same dynamics model.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes attack the weakest metrics (smoothness_score 0.06, slope_changes,           │
│                          │ false_reversals) while preserving the strong ones (correlation 0.93, avg_error 0.23).     │
