│ patch_description        │ Prior gens failed to improve smoothness because post-smoothing was too weak. Add a        │
│                          │ two-pass forward-backward one-pole smoother with alpha ~0.5 applied to the fused output:  │
│                          │ running forward then reversed cancels the lag a single-pass filter would add, so lag      │
│                          │ error stays near 0.22 while the noise-driven ripple (which drives                         │
│                          │ slope_changes/false_reversals) is damped by roughly a factor of 2. The bidirectional      │
│                          │ application is the key: a forward-only pass with the same strength would add phase delay, │
│                          │ but the mirror pass compensates it.                                                       │
