│ patch_description        │ The current program's weakest metric is smoothness (0.06), while lag error is excellent   │
│                          │ (0.22). Prior generations failed because post-smoothing was too weak. This version keeps  │
│                          │ the adaptive forward/backward Kalman fusion (which drives correlation 0.96, noise         │
│                          │ reduction 0.70, low lag) and adds a genuine zero-lag post-smoother: a two-pass            │
│                          │ forward-backward one-pole exponential smoother with α ≈ 0.5 applied to the fused signal.  │
│                          │ Running the one-pole filter forward and then on the reversed sequence cancels the phase   │
│                          │ lag a causal one-pole would introduce, so smoothing strength can be substantial without   │
│                          │ increasing lag error. A second mild forward-backward pass (α = 0.65) further damps        │
│                          │ residual ripple. Output windowing/alignment is unchanged, preserving the same I/O         │
│                          │ contract.                                                                                 │
