│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zerophase_sg_bidirectional                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ A completely different approach: instead of causal state-space smoothing (Kalman/RTS) or  │
│                          │ sliding-window endpoint polynomial fits, this uses zero-phase offline smoothing. First, a │
│                          │ symmetric Savitzky-Golay filter (order 3, adaptive odd window derived from window_size)   │
│                          │ is applied to the whole signal. Savitzky-Golay performs local least-squares polynomial    │
│                          │ regression, which preserves higher-order moments (peaks, trends) far better than moving   │
│                          │ averages while suppressing noise, and because it is symmetric it introduces zero phase    │
│                          │ distortion. Second, a bidirectional (forward + reversed) one-pole exponential smoother    │
│                          │ with moderate alpha (~0.5) further damps residual ripple; running it forward and then     │
│                          │ backward cancels the lag a causal one-pole would add, keeping lag error minimal. The      │
│                          │ result is sliced so output index i corresponds to input time i + window_size - 1,         │
│                          │ preserving the exact input/output contract. Zero-phase processing combined with           │
│                          │ polynomial trend preservation should dramatically reduce slope changes and false          │
│                          │ reversals (already the biggest weaknesses) while maintaining tracking accuracy and        │
│                          │ responsiveness, and it runs in O(n).                                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
