│ patch_name               │ true_rts_smoother_variant                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current code fuses an independent forward and backward Kalman filter with heuristic   │
│                          │ velocity-confidence weights. Replace this with a proper Rauch-Tung-Striebel (RTS)         │
│                          │ smoother: store the filtered states and covariances from the forward pass, then run the   │
│                          │ true backward recursion using the smoother gain G = P_f F' P_pred^{-1}, where P_pred is   │
│                          │ the *predicted* (prior) covariance at each step. The RTS smoother is the minimum-variance │
│                          │ fixed-interval estimate for the linear-Gaussian model, so it should reduce noise and      │
│                          │ false reversals further while keeping zero phase, at the same O(n) cost. Also store       │
│                          │ predicted covariances during the forward pass so the backward recursion is exact. The     │
│                          │ adaptive measurement-noise heuristic is kept, which makes this an adaptive RTS smoother.  │
│                          │ Output slicing and length contract remain unchanged.                                      │
