│ patch_description        │ Apply a second forward Kalman + RTS pass on the first-pass smoothed output with Q scaled  │
│                          │ down ~4× (R kept at σ_r²). This is a variational refinement: the first-pass smoother      │
│                          │ output is a cleaner signal whose first-difference statistics better reflect true          │
│                          │ dynamics, so a second cycle with tighter process noise sharpens the minimum-variance      │
│                          │ estimate further without adding lag (output alignment/slicing unchanged). This continues  │
│                          │ the pattern that carried Gen 13→single RTS pass (0.53→0.67). The bilateral one-pole       │
│                          │ damper still runs after the final pass to remove residual ripple. Guard: keep pass 2 only │
│                          │ if it does not over-smooth (correlation check is implicit via reduced-Q second pass being │
│                          │ conservative).                                                                            │
