│ patch_description        │ The best program (0.72) used the iterated RTS refinement pass and achieved smoothness     │
│                          │ 0.50 with only 20.4 slope changes and 14.2 false reversals, while current program (0.67)  │
│                          │ lost that. Rather than only restoring the refinement, I also tighten the                  │
│                          │ acceleration-noise calibration per feedback: increase the floor from 0.05·σ_r to 0.10·σ_r │
│                          │ and tighten the cap from 0.6·σ_r to 0.4·σ_r. This shrinks Q so the Kalman/RTS smoother    │
│                          │ trusts the constant-velocity model more, suppressing noisy dynamics that cause spurious   │
│                          │ slope changes, at the cost of slightly more lag (0.32 → ~0.34, still excellent). Combined │
│                          │ with restoring the second refinement pass (Q reduced 4x) — which was the single largest   │
│                          │ smoothness gain in the prior best program — this should recover the 0.72-level balance    │
│                          │ and possibly exceed it.                                                                   │
