│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_rts_qfloor_tuned                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replaces the sliding polynomial fit with a bidirectional constant-velocity Kalman         │
│                          │ smoother whose process noise Q is adapted per-sample from local second differences, using │
│                          │ quadrature noise subtraction (local d2 energy minus the noise-only 6σ_r² floor) clipped   │
│                          │ to a tuned floor (0.05σ_r) and cap (0.6σ_r). This shrinks Q where dynamics are            │
│                          │ indistinguishable from noise (fewer slope changes and false reversals) while still        │
│                          │ trusting genuine accelerations (low lag). The fused estimate then passes through zero-lag │
│                          │ bidirectional one-pole smoothers (phase delay cancelled by the mirrored pass) and a       │
│                          │ noise-scaled slope deadzone that flattens sub-noise steps without touching real moves.    │
│                          │ The result targets the weakest metrics — smoothness/slope-change count — while retaining  │
│                          │ the accuracy and responsiveness of the Kalman trend estimate. Interface, output length    │
│                          │ convention, and slicing contract are unchanged.                                           │
