│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ kalman_rts_adaptive_r_hybrid                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the current adaptive-R Kalman/RTS smoother (combined 0.69) with the static-R │
│                          │ variant (combined 0.68). The static-R version achieves better noise reduction (0.63 vs    │
│                          │ 0.59) and correlation, while the adaptive-R version achieves better smoothness (0.42 vs   │
│                          │ 0.39), fewer slope changes and false reversals. The crossover keeps the adaptive          │
│                          │ innovation-based measurement noise from the current program but blends it more strongly   │
│                          │ toward the robust static MAD estimate (0.7*R0 + 0.3*EWMA, slower EWMA λ=0.95), preserving │
│                          │ stability of the smoother while still widening R during noise bursts. The second          │
│                          │ (refinement) RTS pass reverts to the static R from the inspiration program, since the     │
│                          │ refined input is already denoised and a static R there yielded better noise reduction and │
│                          │ accuracy. All other components (adaptive Q from local acceleration, two-pass RTS,         │
│                          │ zero-phase bilateral one-pole ripple damper, output contract) are preserved unchanged.    │
│                          │ This combines the smoothness/reversal advantage of adaptive R with the                    │
│                          │ noise-reduction/accuracy advantage of static R.                                           │
