│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rts_velocity_clamped_smoother                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Key parameters in the current program: the Kalman/RTS process noise (qa, clamped to       │
│                          │ [0.05, 0.6]·σ_r), the Q/4 refinement pass, and the adaptive bidirectional one-pole alpha. │
│                          │ The main weakness is that the RTS smoother's velocity state is discarded. The new         │
│                          │ algorithm keeps the full Kalman/RTS machinery but (1) reduces the process-noise floor so  │
│                          │ the smoother trusts the constant-velocity model more (lower noise on quiet segments →     │
│                          │ fewer false reversals), (2) exploits the smoothed velocity state: after smoothing, a      │
