│ patch_name               │ adaptive_hybrid_kalman_zla_filter                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the strongest elements of the provided scripts: (1) a zero-lag    │
│                          │ Kalman-style adaptive smoothing core that estimates both level and slope (so trend        │
│                          │ direction is preserved with minimal phase delay), (2) an SNR-adaptive gain scheduler that │
│                          │ tightens smoothing in noisy regimes and relaxes it when the signal is clean (preserving   │
│                          │ dynamics), (3) a hysteresis-based trend/reversal detector with slope-change penalty to    │
│                          │ suppress spurious directional flips, and (4) a short polynomial lookahead projection used │
│                          │ only as a gating signal (not output), which improves reversal decisions without           │
│                          │ introducing actual phase lag. The implementation is fully vectorized/online (O(1) per     │
│                          │ sample), minimizing latency while jointly optimizing the four objectives: slope-change    │
│                          │ minimization, lag error, tracking accuracy, and false-reversal penalty.                   │
