│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ localq_rts_pipeline_filter                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign as a staged pipeline around a locally-adaptive-Q Kalman/RTS-style     │
│                          │ smoother. Instead of one global process noise (or a fixed SG window), the algorithm now:  │
│                          │ (1) Hampel-denoises the input, (2) estimates local signal dynamics σ_acc(k) via MAD of    │
│                          │ second differences over 50%-overlapping blocks, linearly interpolates the per-sample      │
│                          │ process noise Q (floored/capped around a reference level) so fast segments (e.g., 5 Hz    │
│                          │ component) get larger Q and slow trend segments get smaller Q, (3) runs a forward         │
│                          │ constant-velocity Kalman pass with per-step Q and innovation-EMA-adaptive R, (4) runs a   │
│                          │ backward pass on the forward estimate with Q scaled 0.25× and blends for zero-phase       │
│                          │ output, and (5) applies a light short-window Savitzky-Golay polish to further cut         │
│                          │ spurious slope reversals. This removes the single global smoothness/responsiveness        │
│                          │ trade-off that caused lag on fast segments while keeping the low slope-change and         │
│                          │ reversal counts, and improves maintainability via small single-responsibility stages.     │
