╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_bidirectional_damper_rts                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This version keeps the original pipeline structure (detrend → noise estimate → RTS        │
│                          │ smoother → bidirectional one-pole damper) but improves the damper stage per feedback:     │
│                          │ lower alpha floor to 0.40 with a lag/correlation guard, and apply two cascaded bilateral  │
│                          │ passes at moderate alpha (0.65) instead of one strong pass. The zero-phase                │
│                          │ (forward-backward) filtering means lower alpha adds no phase delay; smoothing ripple      │
│                          │ (which caps the slope-change score) can therefore be reduced without lag penalty. The     │
│                          │ guard correlates damper output against the pre-damper RTS output; if correlation drops    │
│                          │ below 0.97 the alpha is backed off toward 0.85 to preserve tracking accuracy and prevent  │
│                          │ over-smoothing of genuine dynamics. Cascading two moderate passes flattens the effective  │
│                          │ group-delay/frequency response near the dominant frequencies of the test signals relative │
│                          │ to a single steep pass, improving false-reversal behavior while keeping lag low. All      │
│                          │ inputs/outputs are unchanged.                                                             │
