│                          │ variant measured slightly better slope_changes (29.2 vs 31.6) and false_reversals (23.0   │
│                          │ vs 24.4) while keeping responsiveness identical. From the current program I keep the      │
│                          │ improved ripple damper: the lower alpha floor (0.40), the cascade of two moderate         │
│                          │ bilateral one-pole passes (alpha=0.65) instead of one aggressive pass when heavy          │
│                          │ suppression is requested (flatter group-delay profile, better smoothness without lag),    │
│                          │ and the correlation guard that backs alpha off toward 0.85 if the damper distorts the     │
│                          │ trajectory (protects tracking accuracy). This combines the better noise-adaptation of the │
│                          │ inspiration with the better zero-phase damping of the current program, keeping the same   │
│                          │ I/O contract.                                                                             │
