│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rts_velocity_clamp_fusion                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Fuses the velocity-clamping idea (Gen 41, which delivered the cluster's best smoothness   │
│                          │ 0.56 and fewest false reversals) into the two-pass Kalman/RTS core (Gen 37, superior      │
│                          │ noise reduction). After the second RTS refinement pass and before the zero-phase          │
│                          │ bilateral damper, per-step displacement is clamped using the smoothed velocity state:     │
│                          │ |y−y| ≤ 2·|xs| + slack·σ_r. The clamp is applied in a forward sweep plus a mirrored       │
│                          │ backward sweep so it remains zero-phase (net lag-free). A guard checks correlation        │
│                          │ between clamped and unclamped signals; if corr < 0.97 the slack doubles progressively (up │
│                          │ to effectively disabling) to preserve tracking fidelity. The clamp eliminates             │
│                          │ noise-induced overshoots in per-step displacement — the dominant source of spurious slope │
│                          │ changes and false reversals — without flattening genuine fast dynamics, since genuine     │
│                          │ moves are accompanied by large velocity states and are never clamped.                     │
