│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ local_q_first_pass_plus_tighter_refinement                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The local block-MAD Q currently only affects the refinement pass; the first (noisy-input) │
│                          │ pass still uses the global Q, so busy segments (5 Hz component) are over-smoothed before  │
│                          │ the adaptive pass can recover them — contributing to lag_error (0.34) and avg_error       │
│                          │ (0.39). I propose (1) computing the local block-MAD qseq on the rough moving-average      │
│                          │ trajectory before the first pass and blending it into the first-pass process noise (Q =   │
│                          │ max(local, global)·Qbase), so busy segments get responsive tracking from the start; and   │
│                          │ (2) tightening the refinement pass scale from 0.25 to 0.15 to recover noise_reduction     │
│                          │ (which slipped to 0.55) since the first pass now carries the adaptivity. Block medians    │
│                          │ over the MA-smoothed input remain robust to transients, unlike recursive EWMA estimates.  │
