│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ kalman_rts_velocity_clamp_v2                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program already fuses Gen 37's two-pass Kalman/RTS core with Gen 41's         │
│                          │ zero-phase velocity clamp, scoring 0.72 with smoothness 0.50 and false reversals 14.2.    │
│                          │ The score-ceiling analysis shows smoothness/slope stability is still the dominant lever,  │
│                          │ so this revision pushes three targeted refinements while guarding accuracy:               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Tighter clamp envelope**: The velocity clamp's slack starts at 0.4σ_r (was 0.5) with │
│                          │ the same correlation guard (≥0.97, slack doubling on violation). A tighter envelope       │
│                          │ removes more noise-driven overshoot per step, directly reducing slope changes and false   │
│                          │ reversals.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Third RTS refinement micro-pass**: After the existing blend, one additional          │
│                          │ forward+backward Kalman sweep with Q scaled 8× down and measurement noise re-estimated    │
│                          │ from the already-smoothed signal polishes residual ripple without shifting phase (RTS is  │
│                          │ inherently zero-phase). It is blended conservatively (weight ≤ 0.5) so accuracy and       │
│                          │ responsiveness are preserved.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Sub-noise reversal damping post-damper**: After the bilateral one-pole pass, a final │
│                          │ guarded step suppresses step-to-step sign flips whose magnitude is below 2·σ_step (robust │
│                          │ MAD of the output's first differences). Genuine reversals exceed the noise floor and pass │
│                          │ untouched; spurious ripple flips are pulled toward the previous trend, improving          │
│                          │ smoothness and false-reversal metrics at negligible lag cost. A correlation guard (≥0.97) │
│                          │ disables it if it distorts the signal.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All three entry points (`adaptive_filter`, `enhanced_filter_with_trend_preservation`,     │
│                          │ `process_signal`) and the `y` output slice are unchanged, preserving the I/O contract.    │
