│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ whittaker_polish_fixed_lambda                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the final bilateral one-pole damper with a fixed-λ Whittaker–Henderson polish     │
│                          │ (second-order difference penalty) solved via a banded O(n) Cholesky solve. The one-pole   │
│                          │ damper's position-dependent effective smoothing (its exponential memory makes the penalty │
│                          │ non-uniform) leaks residual ripple — the slope-change count of 20.4 is the weakest        │
│                          │ smoothness metric. A constant λ with a second-order difference penalty applies a uniform  │
│                          │ curvature penalty whose passband is flatter in the band of interest, cutting residual     │
│                          │ ripple without the lag a stronger one-pole cascade would add. λ is derived from the       │
│                          │ residual MAD already computed (r_std) and the robust noise scale (sigma_r):               │
│                          │ clip(25·(r_std/σ_r)², 1, 200). The Whittaker system is pentadiagonal (bandwidth 2 per     │
│                          │ side), solved in O(n) with a simple banded Cholesky implementation, keeping runtime       │
│                          │ ≈0.05s. Applied to the full-length signal before the final slice, so the `len(y) = n −    │
│                          │ window_size + 1` contract is preserved.                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0260                                                                                   │
