│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ staged_pipeline_damper_between_rts                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Restructures the monolithic filter into a staged pipeline of small, composable stages     │
│                          │ (noise estimator, RTS smoother engine, inter-pass damper, adaptive-Q refinement, guarded  │
│                          │ final damper). The key structural change follows the recommendation: the moderate-alpha   │
│                          │ (0.65) zero-phase bilateral damper is moved between the two RTS passes — it removes       │
│                          │ ripple before the Q/4 refinement pass, whose minimum-variance smoothing then re-sharpens  │
│                          │ corners without reintroducing the removed ripple. The RTS engine is factored into a       │
│                          │ reusable function (eliminating the duplicated forward/backward code), process noise       │
│                          │ becomes locally adaptive via robust block-MAD statistics interpolated per sample, and the │
│                          │ final damper keeps a correlation guard. This improves maintainability and targets         │
│                          │ slope-change/false-reversal metrics while keeping lag low.                                │
