│ patch_description        │ Add a dynamics-blended third RTS pass. Gen 35's full-replacement third pass over-smoothed │
│                          │ genuine turns; instead, run a third forward+RTS cycle with q3 = 0.0625·q2 (continuing the │
│                          │ validated 4× geometric decay), then blend y ← y2 + w(k)·(y3 − y2) where w(k) =            │
│                          │ tanh-squashed ratio of local |second difference of y2| to σ_r. In noise-dominated         │
│                          │ segments w→1 (accept the extra smoothing), near genuine turns w→0 (preserve dynamics). A  │
│                          │ convergence gate skips the pass when the second pass already converged, protecting the    │
│                          │ 0.05s runtime budget. This should reduce slope_changes and false_reversals further        │
│                          │ (toward Gen 35's smoothness) while retaining the responsiveness/lag of the current        │
│                          │ generation.                                                                               │
