│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ velocity_clamped_rts_whittaker                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Builds on the best prior program (two-pass Kalman/RTS with locally adaptive per-sample    │
│                          │ process noise + zero-phase Whittaker polish) and adds the recommended velocity-aware      │
│                          │ displacement clamp: after the second RTS refinement pass, a forward + mirrored backward   │
│                          │ clamp limits per-step displacement |y−y| ≤ 2·|v| + slack·σ_r, where v is the smoother's   │
│                          │ own velocity state and slack is expanded if a correlation guard (corr < 0.97 vs.          │
│                          │ unclamped) fires. This directly suppresses noise-induced slope reversals (the dominant    │
│                          │ composite levers: smoothness 0.50, false reversals 14.2) while genuine trend steps pass   │
│                          │ untouched because the velocity state is large there — the clamp is effectively zero-phase │
│                          │ since it's applied symmetrically. The Whittaker banded polish with constant lambda        │
│                          │ replaces the cascaded one-pole damper for flatter passband / sharper ripple stopband.     │
