│ patch_name               │ stage_pipeline_flip_eliminator                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign: the monolithic filter is reorganized into a declarative pipeline of  │
│                          │ self-contained stages (NoiseModel → RTS smoother → flip eliminator → guarded damper →     │
│                          │ output contract), each stage a pure function with its own correlation guard. The key      │
│                          │ change is replacing magnitude-shrinking reversal suppression with a true flip eliminator: │
│                          │ when the pre-damp difference sequence opposes the prevailing trend and its magnitude is   │
│                          │ below a robust noise threshold, the step is held (keep=0) or the two conflicting steps    │
│                          │ are averaged, applied in a forward sweep plus a mirrored backward sweep for zero net      │
│                          │ phase. This eliminates the sub-threshold sign reversals that previously survived          │
│                          │ shrinking (only their amplitude was reduced), directly attacking slope_changes and        │
│                          │ false_reversals while the corr≥0.97 guard with a keep=0.5 retry preserves genuine         │
│                          │ dynamics and tracking accuracy.                                                           │
