│ patch_description        │ Add a guarded zero-phase curvature clamp as the missing complement to the velocity clamp. │
│                          │ The current pipeline bounds per-step displacement but permits alternating ±limit steps    │
│                          │ (oscillation entirely within the displacement bound), which is exactly how ~20 slope      │
│                          │ changes survive. Clamping the second difference |y − 2y + y| ≤ c·(robust d2 scale of the  │
│                          │ current output) in forward+backward sweeps directly bounds the derivative's oscillation   │
│                          │ rate without adding lag or shifting the level. A correlation guard (≥ 0.97,               │
│                          │ slack-doubling retry like the velocity clamp) prevents distortion of genuine fast         │
│                          │ dynamics. Genuine curvature of the smoothed signal is far larger than residual noise      │
│                          │ curvature, so c ≈ 1.5 passes real turns while killing residual ripple.                    │
