│ patch_description        │ Structural re-architecture: the processing is organized as an explicit, modular pipeline  │
│                          │ (noise estimation → RTS pass 1 → inter-pass bilateral damper → RTS Q/4 refinement →       │
│                          │ guarded reversal damping), implementing the key untested lever: the zero-phase one-pole   │
│                          │ damper is moved BETWEEN the two RTS passes (alpha ≈ 0.72) instead of running after both.  │
│                          │ This removes ripple early so the Q/4 refinement pass re-sharpens genuine corners that the │
│                          │ damper rounds, while removed ripple stays removed — reducing slope changes and false      │
│                          │ reversals without the lag cost of terminal damper stacking (which caps at 0.65–0.68 per   │
│                          │ Gens 42/45). A lag monitor re-checks residual MAD and gates a light terminal polish       │
│                          │ (alpha=0.9) only when residual ripple exceeds 0.3·σ_r. The velocity clamp is dropped (it  │
│                          │ produced no improvement) and the code is reorganized into a clean, reusable               │
│                          │ stage-function architecture with a single RTS engine function, improving maintainability  │
│                          │ and efficiency.                                                                           │
