│ patch_name               │ stage_pipeline_flip_elim_whittaker                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign into a modular three-stage pipeline: (1) robust statistics stage      │
│                          │ (MAD-based noise/acceleration estimation), (2) banded Whittaker smoother stage (O(n)      │
│                          │ pentadiagonal solve, uniform lambda with local curvature relaxation), and (3) a new       │
│                          │ flip-elimination damper that fixes the polarity flaw of prior reversal dampers: instead   │
│                          │ of shrinking sub-threshold sign flips (keep=0.25, which preserved the flip's sign), it    │
│                          │ removes them entirely by zeroing the conflicting difference and holding the line. Applied │
│                          │ as a forward sweep plus mirrored backward sweep (zero-phase), with prev_d tracked from    │
│                          │ pre-damp differences to avoid zero-stall, and a corr>=0.97 guard with keep=0.5 retry.     │
│                          │ This directly attacks slope_changes and false_reversals while keeping lag low via the     │
│                          │ zero-phase banded solve.                                                                  │
