│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ gen53_style_core_with_guarded_suppressor                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Per the recommendation, this revision interpolates the core smoother toward Gen 53's      │
│                          │ proven high-accuracy operating point while keeping the guarded suppressor stack (velocity │
│                          │ clamp + reversal damper + bilateral one-pole) fully intact. Changes vs the current        │
│                          │ program:                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Centered Hampel despiker** (window 7, threshold 3·local-MAD) applied to the input    │
│                          │ before the Kalman pass, mirroring Gen 53's preprocessing. Skipped entirely if >5% of      │
│                          │ samples are flagged (degenerate/very noisy input) to avoid distorting genuine dynamics.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Acceleration-noise cap raised** from `0.6·sigma_r` to `0.85·sigma_r`, letting the    │
│                          │ process noise track genuine fast dynamics more faithfully. This is the single biggest     │
│                          │ lever toward Gen 53's correlation 0.97 / noise-reduction 0.81 / lag 0.28.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Blend floor lowered** from `w_refine ≥ 0.25` to `w_refine ≥ 0.10` (`clip(1.25 −      │
│                          │ 1.25·dyn_ratio, 0.10, 1.0)`), so even in dynamic-heavy segments the sharper refinement    │
│                          │ pass dominates, improving noise reduction and tracking accuracy.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Critically, the final dampers are NOT removed: the guarded velocity clamp                 │
│                          │ (correlation-guarded slack relaxation), the guarded sub-noise reversal damper, and the    │
│                          │ guarded bilateral one-pole all remain. Gen 43/52 showed that responsive cores without     │
│                          │ terminal suppression collapse to smoothness ~0.17 with ~70 reversals; the guard stack is  │
│                          │ what keeps reversals near 14 while the more responsive core lifts                         │
│                          │ correlation/noise-reduction/lag toward the Gen 53 point. Expected net: correlation        │
│                          │ ~0.92–0.94, noise reduction ~0.65+, lag ~0.31, with reversals still suppressed by the     │
│                          │ terminal stack — a combined score above the current 0.72.                                 │
