│ patch_description        │ Terminal polish stages (dampers, reversal-damp escalation) have plateaued: prior          │
│                          │ generations varied only terminal damper strength with zero metric movement. The one       │
│                          │ untested structural lever is ordering. Replace the third micro-refinement pass (fixed     │
│                          │ Q/8, R from residual) with an adaptive-Q/8 pass that uses a locally adaptive block-MAD    │
│                          │ qseq estimated on the blended signal, and move the velocity clamp earlier — between pass  │
│                          │ 2 and pass 3 — so the refinement pass re-sharpens corners the clamp rounds while removed  │
│                          │ overshoot stays removed. The adaptive Q/8 estimates local second-difference energy per    │
│                          │ block, so quiet regions get more smoothing (fewer slope changes/false reversals) while    │
│                          │ dynamic regions get near-zero extra smoothing (lag preserved). The corridor monitor: if   │
│                          │ lag_error proxy (residual robust std of the final output's first differences relative to  │
│                          │ sigma_r) indicates over-smoothing, blend down w3. This targets the slope_changes (20.40)  │
│                          │ and false_reversals (14.20) metrics without touching lag_error (0.34) or accuracy (0.89). │
