│ patch_name               │ interpass_damper_and_gated_polish                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation identifies the one structural lever never tested: placing a bilateral  │
│                          │ one-pole damper *between* the two RTS passes rather than as terminal polish. Rationale:   │
│                          │ the Q/4 (locally adaptive) refinement pass re-sharpens genuine corners that the damper    │
│                          │ rounds — its Kalman gain responds to real dynamics — while removed ripple stays removed.  │
│                          │ This decouples smoothness from the accuracy guard that caps smoothness at 0.50.           │
│                          │ Additionally, the terminal Whittaker polish is gated on substantial residual ripple       │
│                          │ (r_std > 0.3·sigma_r): polishing a clean output only adds lag and risk of trend loss.     │
│                          │ Alpha for the inter-pass damper is set ~0.70 (within the recommended 0.65–0.75 band),     │
│                          │ tuned from the pass-1 residual ripple scale.                                              │
