│ patch_name               │ soft_quadratic_reversal_damp                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the hard hold (keep=0.0) in the guarded reversal damping with a                   │
│                          │ magnitude-proportional quadratic soft damp: out = out + d*(1 - (|d|/thresh)^2) for        │
│                          │ sub-threshold flips. The hard hold creates flat zero-step segments that inflate           │
│                          │ avg_error/lag while leaving residual flips from the mirrored backward sweep               │
│                          │ re-introducing what the forward sweep removed. The quadratic falloff pins tiny flips to   │
│                          │ (nearly) zero while passing near-threshold steps almost intact, so a single unguarded     │
│                          │ sweep pair suffices — no guard retry escalation (which previously halted smoothing too    │
│                          │ early at the 0.97 correlation check). Guard instead with a single hard abort: correlation │
│                          │ against the original input slice must stay >= 0.93, otherwise revert to the pre-damp      │
│                          │ signal. All sanitization and the rest of the pipeline remain untouched.                   │
