│ patch_description        │ A fundamentally different approach: instead of Kalman/RTS state-space filtering, use a    │
│                          │ zero-phase Savitzky-Golay local polynomial smoother (centered, so no phase lag by         │
│                          │ construction) with an adaptive effective smoothing scale derived from a robust MAD noise  │
│                          │ estimate, fused via a dynamics-aware blend with a running-median pre-pass. The median     │
│                          │ pre-pass removes impulsive noise that least-squares polynomials would smear; the          │
│                          │ Savitzky-Golay pass then fits genuine local dynamics exactly (polynomials reproduce       │
│                          │ polynomial trends), giving strong noise reduction with minimal lag. A light bidirectional │
│                          │ one-pole finish damps residual ripple. Centers near the boundaries use shorter asymmetric │
│                          │ polynomial windows so every output sample is supported by real data. This avoids the      │
│                          │ Kalman lag/overshoot trade-off and the flat-segment artifacts of reversal clamps,         │
